# Bot quality evaluation gateway

**Regression testing**, **golden questions**, **RAG_TURN_AUDIT forensics**, and **expected-answer checks** must follow **`.cursor/skills/bot-quality-evaluation`**.

## Load the skill when the user asks to

- Test whether the bot answered correctly
- Investigate a bad Teams turn (prod or dev)
- Run golden / acceptance-criteria checks
- Compare retrieval vs expected documents

## If the skill is not loaded

1. Read `.cursor/skills/bot-quality-evaluation/SKILL.md` before KQL, pytest, or `run_local_rag_tests.py`.
2. Use [acceptance-criteria.md](../../.cursor/skills/bot-quality-evaluation/acceptance-criteria.md), not ad-hoc expectations.

## Coordination

| Finding | Skill |
|---------|--------|
| Corpus / index fix | `knowledge-base-curator` |
| Ship fix to Azure | `deployment-ops` |

**Scripts:** `scripts/bot.sh`, `scripts/kql.sh`. **Runtime:** `bot-test` / `dev` — see skill workflow.

**Narrow exception:** filling `pinecone-pipeline/agent_exports/` tables only — skill § Corpus Q&A export; no live bot eval required.
